<h1>For My Dear Goddaughter, Hailey's First Holy Communion</h1><br/><br/><strong>
<br/>
Angels and saints silently gather to sing songs of glorious delight.<br/>
Family and friends joyfully tie smiling happy wishes to soaring, sky high kites.<br/>
Sunday, May 7, 2006 is whitest, brightest, and happiest in every way<br/>
For it is your long awaited First Holy Communion Day!<br/>
You are dressed all in pure white and you have tried to do what is just right.<br/>
Jesus is excited as He waits for you expectantly in the beautiful box with the light.<br/>
Prayerfully place your hopes and dreams on the golden paten that the priest will raise<br/>
Give thanks to God for His Son's Holy Sacrifice on the altar and offer all your praise<br/>
Good and gentle Jesus will be really and truly present in the small, round Host<br/>
Sweet Jesus will softly kiss your soul because He loves you, His little child, the most.<br/>
You, dear Hailey, will take sweet Jesus into your clean and pure heart.<br/>
 Joy, Grace, and Spirited gifts, He will generously and gladly impart.<br/>
So remember to talk to Jesus, your Friend forever, while He is inside of you.<br/>
Ask Him to help you to love Him more and more in everything you do.<br/>
Then silently listen to the precious Lamb of God lovingly whisper back to you.<br/>
Give praise to Him, His Father, and the Holy Spirit the whole perfect day through!<br/>
<br/>
